Under RBI rules, recovery agents of banks/NBFCs:
- may call or visit only **between 8 am and 7 pm**;
- must show **ID and an authorisation letter**;
- must not threaten, abuse, humiliate, or contact your relatives/friends to shame you.

**What to do:** note dates/times, record calls if possible, complain in writing to the lender's grievance officer, then to the **RBI Ombudsman (cms.rbi.org.in, 14448)** if not resolved in 30 days. Physical threats are crimes — call **100/112**.
